# Product direction

Read [`docs/DIRECTION.md`](docs/DIRECTION.md), [`docs/CGI-VARIANTS.md`](docs/CGI-VARIANTS.md), [`docs/COST.md`](docs/COST.md), [`docs/SECURITY.md`](docs/SECURITY.md).

- **Target:** shared hosting CGI (upload one static binary), not VPS/long-lived servers.
- **Default:** `sync-cgi` / `marty::Router`. Prefer this for new examples, APIs, and docs.
- **Axum/`tower`:** optional for existing Axum handlers via `serve_cgi` — not the primary DX; do not aim for Axum feature parity in the sync router.
- **CGI variants:** document + Docker-mirror (hosting-like first, prefork as lab); do not reintroduce prefork-only library hacks (e.g. pacing).
- **Claims about hosting:** prefer `benchmarks/complex` (`just outside` / hosting Docker) + `tools/hosting-probe`; verified hosts Oct 2026: all-inkl + Hetzner Webhosting S (cgid sockets, Run N) + netcup EiWoMiSau (pipe/mod_cgi behind nginx, Run O) — [`HOSTERS.md`](docs/HOSTERS.md); cloud vs hosting complex: [`alternatives/RESULTS-SNAPSHOTS.md`](alternatives/RESULTS-SNAPSHOTS.md) (Hetzner ≈ CF top warm P50); do not treat prefork-only Docker benches as truth for socket hosts (netcup is pipe-class).
- **`.htaccess`:** feature `htaccess` — alias in `[package.metadata.marty]`, binary = package name; `write_next_to_binary_from_manifest` → `{binary}.htaccess`; `just linux` → `target/deploy/<pkg>/`.
